---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { company } from '../data/links';
import { organizationLd } from '../data/seo';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy | Elinsoft"
  description="How the elinsoft.co.uk website treats your data: Google Analytics only if you accept, no advertising, no forms."
  path="/privacy"
  jsonLd={[organizationLd()]}
>
  <div class="container page">
    <p class="draft" role="note"><strong>Draft.</strong> This page is a draft for the owner to review and has not been approved yet.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h1 class="page__title">Privacy<span class="stop">.</span></h1>
      <p>
        This page explains what happens to your data when you visit <strong>elinsoft.co.uk</strong>. It covers this website
        only, not our apps.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Google Analytics runs only if you press "Accept analytics". If you press "Reject", or do not choose, nothing is sent to Google Analytics.</li>
        <li>No advertising scripts.</li>
        <li>If you press play on the trailer, YouTube may store data in your browser.</li>
        <li>No forms, accounts or sign-ups: we do not ask you for any personal information on this site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        If you press "Accept analytics", we use Google Analytics 4 to see how the site is used. Our lawful basis is your
        consent. It collects the pages you view, how you arrived, your device and browser type, your approximate location
        (derived from your IP address) and the time you spend on a page.
      </p>
      <p>
        It sets the cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, which last for up to 2 years. Google acts as our
        processor and may process data outside the UK. We do not run advertising, so all advertising consent settings stay
        denied.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can change your mind at any time with the "Cookie settings" link in the footer of every page. Choosing "Reject"
        stops analytics and deletes the cookies it set.
      </p>

      <h2>What other services see</h2>
      <p>
        The site is delivered by Cloudflare. Like any web host, it handles your IP address and the usual details of a
        request (the page you asked for, your browser type) to deliver the page and keep the service secure.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site's fonts (Fraunces and Inter) are loaded from Google Fonts, so your browser makes a request to Google's font
        servers, which means Google also receives your IP address. Nothing else on the page contacts a third party when it
        loads.
      </p>
      <p>
        When a trailer video is shown on the Dino page, it only loads after you press play, and then from YouTube's
        privacy-enhanced domain (youtube-nocookie.com).
      </p>

      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us at <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>, we use your address and message only to
        reply to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        {company.name}, company number {company.number}, registered in {company.jurisdiction}. Registered office: {company.registeredOffice}.
      </p>
      <p>You can also contact us to ask about your data. If you are in the UK, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).</p>

      <p class="page__date">Last updated: 26 November 2026 (draft).</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: 24px 80px;
  }

  .draft {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border: 2px dashed #b27a00;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .page__title {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 8vw, 3.75rem);
  }

  .page__date {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
</style>
